# Line endings are part of this repo's contract, not a local preference. Without these rules the
# cloning machine's core.autocrlf decides, and both file-convention invariants break in opposite
# directions - silently, because the test suite still passes with a converted fixture.

# Every .ps1 must arrive CRLF on every platform. docs/STATUS.md states this as an invariant.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Fixtures are byte-exact test data. tests/fixtures/newlines/ is deliberately LF-only and its
# embedded newline is the thing under test; any conversion destroys the coverage. -text disables
# EOL translation entirely while still diffing as text.
tests/fixtures/** -text

# Baselines (TEST-PLAN.md Group D) are byte-exact recordings of real script output - CRLF because
# the scripts themselves always write CRLF. Same reasoning as tests/fixtures/** above: without
# -text, a clone under a different core.autocrlf could silently convert them, and the comparison
# that reads them is byte/hash-based, not EOL-tolerant.
tests/baselines/** -text

# Docs are LF.
*.md text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
